From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:42:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] SEO: 11 subject sub-hubs and data-driven hub text

New static, prerendered pages under the category hubs, each with its own
title, H1, intro, filtered list of indexable listings, FAQ (with FAQPage
JSON-LD), ItemList and BreadcrumbList JSON-LD, sitemap entry and a link from
its parent hub:

  /categories/competitions/{stem,science,math,research,
    business-entrepreneurship,writing-essay}
  /categories/internships/{medical,law}
  /categories/summer-programs/{business,free,nyc}

Online-only internships (3 listings) are left to /remote. Counts, free vs
paid, deadline months and grade facts are computed from the listings, so the
'At a glance' text and FAQ answers cannot drift from the catalogue. The six
category hubs gain the same 'At a glance' text (now 325-378 words) and
'Browse by subject' links to their sub-hubs and matching guides.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015eydvdzcxBPZCXsPy7MGLS
